import json
from pathlib import Path
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;r=json.loads((P/'results.json').read_text())
lines=['# Audit of supplied perpetuals research','','## Conclusion','','Use the BTC spot/perpetual funding hedge as a concrete mechanism-driven research candidate. It is a materially different thesis from unhedged funding fade or price-direction rules. The funding bias is verified and the matched-price historical proxy supports positive net carry under several explicit fee scenarios. The provided note overstates certainty, understates collateral under its own leverage policy, and compares annualized yield to a one-time cost misleadingly. At$100, expected dollar scale is cents over weeks, not meaningful frequent-bet income. No position, hedge, transfer or recurring service was created.','','## Verified from cached history and new independent spot data','',f"BTC funding:{r['positive']} positive/{r['negative']} negative/{r['zero']} zero across{r['funding_count']} records. Sum{100*r['sum_rates']:.4f}% over{r['days']:.2f}days. Simple annualization{100*r['simple_annualized']:.2f}% on constant notional, not on all committed capital and not a forecast. The fixed7day blocks in this audit are all positive. The exact weekly figures in the pasted note are not reproduced by our window boundaries; our final trailing7days have21payments totaling{100*r['trailing7']['rate_sum']:.4f}%, equivalent to{100*r['trailing7']['annualized']:.2f}% annualized. Compression is supported.",'','Current account fee receipt confirms crypto2/12bp maker/taker and metals0.12/0.72bp. Metals trading fees are16.67times lower for the same notional and order type. That is a cost advantage, not an arbitrage profit by itself. Funding signs/ratios do not establish why the imbalance exists or whether competing arbitrageurs are absent. The claim that nobody is arbitraging it is unsupported.','','## Actual fixed-unit hedge diagnostic','','Short5BTCperp contracts and buy0.0005BTC spot. Match units rather than repeatedly rebalance dollar notionals as the price moves: linear spot and linear perpetual deltas already move together. Rebalance for partial fills, contract changes or position mismatches, not simply because BTC price changed.','','Use Aug8 first common hourly close to Sep26 last common close. Kalshi perp bid/ask closes are matched with Coinbase BTC-USD candle closes; Coinbase candles are last trades, not executable bid/ask quotes. This is an approximate basis/fee diagnostic. Maker scenario assumes favorable fills at quoted prices and has no fill proof. Spot fee levels are scenarios because the user’s actual spot-exchange tier was not accessed.','','Entry spot cost~$32.45; short notional~$32.44. Reserving one times short notional plus the spot purchase uses~$64.89, leaving~$35.11of a$100budget before fees. Prices later rose, so this historical entry capital differs from a current5contract position. Gross observed funding is$0.6628; the taker-price basis/crossing component is−$0.004985.','','| Perp execution | Spot fee per side | Perp fees | Spot fees | Net before spot spread/other costs |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for x in r['hedge_scenarios']:
 if x['contracts']==5 and x['spot_fee_bp_per_side'] in [10,40,60,120]:lines.append(f"| {x['execution']} | {x['spot_fee_bp_per_side']/100:.2f}% | ${x['perpfees']:.4f} | ${x['spotfees']:.4f} | ${x['net_before_spot_spread_and_other_costs']:+.4f} |")
lines+=['','These are not annual returns or live realized gains. Spot spreads, transfer/withdrawal costs, minimum-size rounding, interest/opportunity cost, taxes and operational failures are not included. A better actual fee tier helps, but assumed maker fills cannot be treated as certain.','',f"Across{r['historical_basis_proxy_bp']['observations']} matched hourly observations, the perp-vs-Coinbase-close basis proxy has median{r['historical_basis_proxy_bp']['median']:.2f}bp, absolute90th percentile{r['historical_basis_proxy_bp']['p90_abs']:.2f}bp and range{r['historical_basis_proxy_bp']['min']:.2f}to{r['historical_basis_proxy_bp']['max']:.2f}bp. This uses unsynchronized last-trade/quote values and cannot verify subsecond tradable basis or statistical stationarity. It supports small endpoint basis in this particular test, not a guaranteed constant premium.",'','## Corrections to the proposed design','','1. “Never take price risk” is too strong. Matched BTC units reduce common BTC price exposure, but venue basis, hedge execution gaps, liquidity, contract/mark methodology, custody and liquidation remain. Spot gains at another venue do not automatically collateralize a losing Kalshi short.','2. The note says run at<=2x but budgets~$1600margin against$10000short notional. That is~6.25x. A2x ceiling requires at least$5000perp collateral plus$10000spot plus buffer. Full1x collateral requires$10000for the short plus$10000spot. Returns must be measured on this full capital, not perp notional alone.',f"3. In the historical5contract example, BTC rose as much as{100*r['btc_spot_max_move_from_entry']:.1f}% from entry and the short leg’s worst observed bid/ask P&L including funding was${r['short_leg_worst_unrealized_5contracts']:.2f}. An external winning hedge does not remove this margin cash need. No maintenance-margin/liquidation calculation is claimed.",f"4. Comparing8.5% annualized funding to0.24% one-time fees as ‘35times’ hides the holding period. At the freshly calculated{100*r['trailing7']['annualized']:.2f}% annualized rate, perp taker fees alone need about{r['trailing7']['taker_perp_fee_only_breakeven_days']:.0f}days of unchanged funding. Including0.40%spot fees on entry and exit takes about{r['trailing7']['with40bp_spot_each_side_breakeven_days']:.0f}days before spreads or basis. Rate compression can lengthen this.",'5. A funding exit rule needs costs and hysteresis. An arbitrary annualized floor can churn away carry through repeated hedge unwinds. Evaluate expected remaining funding against full entry/exit costs, declining rates and available collateral; do not treat past annualization as a guaranteed future rate.','6. Use the actual estimated/historical funding endpoints and explicit timestamps. Crypto and metals payment schedules differ. Validate received account cashflows against estimates before assigning yield.','7. Same-venue shortBTC/XRP versus longWLD/ADA is a different speculative spread trade. Equal dollars is not equal beta or a same-asset hedge; dispersion can overwhelm carry. It is not a substitute for cash-and-carry.','','## What to incorporate from the notes','','Adopt: dynamically read effective account fee rates; price executable orders from timestamped books; reject empty/sentinel books; preserve a proper same-asset hedge; reconcile unit delta and funding; model funding compression; keep leverage/collateral arithmetic internally consistent. Trading-hours differences in metals and fast-reference maker strategies are research hypotheses, not established profits. Our prior small book sample showed positive spread-minus-maker-fee room in metals/LTC but did not test queue fills or adverse selection.','','Do not automatically discard all unusual candles or use robust statistics to hide real crashes. Validate invalid/sentinel quotes separately from legitimate large moves. Stops, sizing and stress tests need the latter. The prior directional results were concentrated in an August rally and were not independent confirmations of an edge. The note’s aggregated multi-strategy profits must not be interpreted as achievable on one$100portfolio.','','## Decision for this account size','','The BTC hedge is worth a cost-and-execution feasibility experiment; prioritize it over unhedged “funding capture.” It is a slow carry strategy, not a practical way to generate many meaningful profits from$100. A technically sound research prototype would record paired executable quotes, actual spot fee tier, perps funding estimates and hedge-unit reconciliation without trading. Live use is not supported until paired fills, costs and collateral stress are validated. This audit creates research artifacts only.','','## Sources and reproduction','','- [Coinbase Advanced fees](https://help.coinbase.com/en/coinbase/trading-and-funding/advanced-trade/advanced-trade-fees): exact tier depends on account; modeled tiers here are assumptions.','- [Kalshi funding](https://help.kalshi.com/en/articles/15357613-how-funding-works)','- [Kalshi perpetual fee explanation](https://help.kalshi.com/en/articles/16071417-perps-fees-explained)','- Input perp history/funding: ../kalshi_perps_expanded_2026_09_26/data. New Coinbase hourly observations are in data/. results.json retains all scenarios, weekly calculations and basis diagnostics.','- Formula: short-perp P&L + equal-BTC-unit spot P&L + actual funding − perp fees − assumed spot fees. Existing quotes are not proof of fills. No future rate was used for a claimed causal entry/exit rule: this is a fixed-period retrospective hedge diagnostic.']
(P/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n');print('report saved')
